From 2d66f07120076d3f0778a6629be2b2ba86f50be3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:35:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(oslexec): preserve signatures for native closure
 callbacks

Native closure prepare and setup callbacks are constant function
pointers, not LLVM Function objects. Keep their explicit function
signature when emitting scalar and batched calls instead of interpreting
an opaque pointer as a Function.

Retain the direct-call overload and add JIT tests for indirect integer
results and closure-style prepare/setup callbacks. All 25 selected
closure and LLVM utility tests pass.

